    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nNet rate of radiative heat exchange between a real body at temperature T and surrounding enclosure at T₀ is P_net = e σ A (T⁴ - T₀⁴).\n\n2. GIVEN:\ne = 0.80, A = 0.050 m², T = 500 K, T₀ = 300 K, σ = 5.67 × 10⁻⁸ W/(m²·K⁴).\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nP_{\\text{net}} = e \\sigma A (T^4 - T_0^4)\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. T⁴ = (500)⁴ = 6.2500e+10 K⁴.\n2. T₀⁴ = (300)⁴ = 8.1000e+09 K⁴.\n3. (T⁴ - T₀⁴) = 5.4400e+10 K⁴.\n4. P_net = (0.80) × (5.67 × 10⁻⁸) × (0.050) × (5.4400e+10) = 123.38 W.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: 123.38 W\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nCRITICAL TRAP: (T⁴ - T₀⁴) is NEVER equal to (T - T₀)⁴! Always calculate individual fourth powers.",
