    "question": "Assuming the Sun radiates as a blackbody at temperature 5800 K with radius R_s = 7.0 × 10⁸ m, calculate the solar constant S received at Earth's orbital distance d = 1.496 × 10¹¹ m. (Take σ = 5.67 × 10⁻⁸ W/(m²·K⁴))",
